# E339 draft - OHOS test_package CMake helper PATH closure

id:                     E529
trigger_tool:           conan test_package|CMake.configure|cmake
phase:                  validation
error_signature:        /system/bin/sh: cmake: inaccessible or not found|CMake.configure.*Error 127|test package.*cmake

severity:               3
category:               ohos, cmake, conan, packaging, testing
match_keywords:         libunwind, test_package, CMake, cmake_layout, VirtualRunEnv, tools.build:compiler_executables, /data/service/hnp/bin, shadow CI
title:                  Give OHOS CMake test_package recipes their own tool PATH

root_cause:             Conan executes test_package as a separate recipe context. Build environment scripts generated by the package recipe do not automatically repair PATH for CMake.configure() inside the test package. On OHOS shadow CI, cmake and make can live in the same native toolchain directory as clang, so a package can build successfully while its consumer test fails with cmake inaccessible or not found.
affected_scope:         Conan 2 test_package recipes using CMake, CMakeToolchain, CMakeDeps, and cmake_layout on OHOS where the runner PATH is minimal and tool locations are primarily exposed through tools.build:compiler_executables.
verification_cmd:       CI_PACKAGES="archives/l/libunwind/1.6.2" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           test-package-local-tool-path
rec_description:        Add a generate() method to the test_package recipe. For OHOS, derive the tool directory from tools.build:compiler_executables['c'], fall back to /data/service/hnp/bin when present, prepend that directory to PATH with Environment(), and save the script before calling CMake.configure().
rec_command:            conan create archives/l/libunwind/1.6.2 --build=missing
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-test-package

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      explicit-cmake-tool-conf
fallback_description:   If a future runner separates cmake from clang, extend the same test_package-local generate() method to read an explicit CMake tool path from Conan conf. Keep the fix in the test package, not in the main package build step.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          conan-test-package

forbid_1_pattern:       skip.*test_package|def test.*pass|return.*before.*CMake
forbid_1_reason:        The CMake failure is an environment closure problem, not evidence that consumer validation should be removed.
forbid_1_consequence:   The package can publish without proving that installed headers and libraries are consumable.
forbid_2_pattern:       assume.*package.*generate.*test_package|source.*conanbuild.*from package cache
forbid_2_reason:        The package recipe and test_package recipe have separate generated environments.
forbid_2_consequence:   The main package build passes, but the consumer test remains non-reproducible.

principles:             P013,P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E338
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

